        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_882e720cc2894818bce5c07aa9a5e9d3",
      "statement": "The ingestion pipeline has six steps: (1) validate type/size/pages/parseability and compute SHA-256, (2) insert-or-get content by hash with four branching outcomes (existing ready → skip extraction and show suggestions; existing processing → document waits; existing failed → re-queue; new hash → proceed), (3) move file to contents/<sha256>.pdf, (4) first-pages step using a describe_document tool call to extract title/authors/year/DOI/summary/subject names and store a summary embedding, (5) subject suggestion ranking by embedding similarity, (6) full Docling extraction saving contents/<sha256>.docling.json and extracting references, work_key, chunks, and embeddings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/src/smart_tutor/knowledge/README.md#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e37ec23ef5a6e64b5055c8e0d24bec2cea4580c9c05be3acd78c0afb47f8855c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/prd.md#L308-L313",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ec478f89f00101b3ad2a688770663fb8ce9456180f0d1c8b41b3f1c975818455:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a5a6f1eea6664f149d1c5524ef900e3e",
      "statement": "Deduplication is enforced server-side via SHA-256 of uploaded bytes only; a browser-sent hash can only skip re-uploading a file already in the same learner's own library but never links a document to another learner's content (PRD D19).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sdd/adr/0002-content-document-split-sha256-dedupe.md#L13-L14",
