    {
      "id": "claim_4c58ed38a8f143fd89ca6982dbd140ab",
      "statement": "Before uploading, the browser computes the SHA-256 of the selected file and calls the API to check whether that hash already appears in the learner's own library; if a match is found the upload is skipped and the learner sees 'Already in your library' (or 'Restore' if archived). This check covers only the learner's own documents; it cannot expose another learner's files (PRD D19).",
      "evidence": [
        {
